        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cc551f44-6425-5926-ae15-6388c42d2b00",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Midge Mackenzie, Kate Millett, Robert Joffrey, Betty Friedan\n- Organizations: Joffrey Ballet, BBC, Oxford University, St Hilda's College\n- Products: Astarte, Women Talking, Shoulder to Shoulder\n- Topics: women's liberation movement, women's suffrage movement\n\nFacts:\n- Midge Mackenzie was born in London on 6 March 1938 and was a writer and filmmaker.\n- Kate Millett attended Oxford University and studied at St Hilda's College, Oxford.\n- Kate Millett was the first American woman to receive a degree with first-class honors at St Hilda's College, Oxford.\n- Midge Mackenzie first became known for producing Robert Joffrey's multimedia ballet Astarte with the Joffrey Ballet.\n- Midge Mackenzie made Women Talking, a documentary featuring interviews with Kate Millett, Betty Friedan, and other leading figures in the U.S. women's liberation movement.\n- In 1974, the BBC television serial Shoulder to Shoulder and its companion book about the history of the women's suffrage movement were both edited by Midge Mackenzie.\n- Midge Mackenzie died on 28 January 2004.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
